.UPDATE...
Issued at 908 AM PDT Thu Jul 30 2026

Satellite imagery shows stratus clouds dissipating across the SF Bay
Area, with a lingering patch on the west side of San Francisco and
the Pacifica area, while the clouds slowly dissipate along the
Salinas Valley and linger around the Monterey Bay region. Today
will mark the first day of a warming period that will bring
temperatures warmer than the seasonal average across the interior
regions into the early part of next week. People sensitive to
heat, including children, the elderly, pregnant women, and those
with certain medical conditions, should stay hydrated and take
breaks in the shade.

