.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1246 AM PDT Thu Jul 30 2026
(Today and tonight)

The marine layer clouds that went "poof" earlier in the evening
are slowly reforming along portions of the coast per satellite fog
product. The N-S gradient from SFO-ACV eased, which is also
assisting with the building stratus. That being said, expect some
stratus coverage along the coast this morning and locally inland,
especially Salinas Valley. Any morning clouds will likely be gone
by mid to late morning.

The much talked about interior warm up will be in fully swing
today. While Wednesday features a few spots in the mid to upper
90s (Pinnacles hit 100) those readings will be a little more
widespread. Why the interior heat? The large area of high pressure
that oppressive heat to the Desert SW has been building westward
for a few days now and today it will be more impactful for our
interior locations. What about the coast? Still no change there.
We`ll see some warmer conditions, AM clouds and onshore flow will
keep temperatures cooler.

Speaking of onshore flow, SFO-SAC will likely eclipse 3mb again
this afternoon, which will bring gusts of 25-40 mph for inland
valleys, gaps, passes.

For tonight, some patchy stratus will once again develop, but
given the robust building 500mb heights the marine layer will be
more compressed.

