.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 225 PM PDT Wed Jul 29 2026

The elevated fire weather threat will continue across portions of
the area through this weekend, and potentially into next week.
Overnight RH recovery will remain moderate to poor at locations at
or above 2,000 feet with values between 35 to 45 percent, with
some favored locations struggling to even reach 30 percent. This
will be particularly true across the Mayacamas, highest peaks of
the East Bay Hills, the Diablo Range, Santa Cruz Mountains, Santa
Lucia and Gabilan Ranges. Nocturnal drying (rapid decrease in RH
through the pre- dawn hours) may also transpire which will
increase the burn period or time in which fire behavior may remain
active. Afternoon RH will remain critically dry with values
between 15 and 30 percent, with far southern portions of the
interior Central Coast potentially seeing min RH near 10 percent.
Energy Release Components (ERC) are projected to climb above the
95th percentile across the interior Central Coast. Individuals
across the area are advised to avoid activities that may spark a
fire. Fire crews are urged to exercise extra caution when
executing any prescribed burns, especially where fuels,
topography, and weather align.

